Vectors for the did_webvh credential (draft-atwood-mls-didwebvh-credential), read by mimihubd's tests
(mimihubd/src/didwebvh_vectors_tests.rs) through the hub's own credential and group-rule code.

vectors.json, vectors.PROVENANCE
  From github.com/MarkAtwood/mimid at 7089317472af8ac5c1da05e36dd8f071e6c32256,
  crates/mls-didwebvh/tests/vectors/ (Apache-2.0). Generated by that directory's generate.mjs, which builds every log,
  witness file and TLS encoding with its own JCS, base58btc, did:webvh v1.0 entry construction and eddsa-jcs-2022 proofs
  (Node built-in crypto only), independently of the Rust crate, and writes each expected outcome from the draft's text.
  vectors.PROVENANCE is that directory's own record, copied unchanged.

dif/<scenario>/
  From the DIF did:webvh test suite, github.com/decentralized-identity/didwebvh-test-suite, commit 703f97f, vectors/
  (Apache-2.0), as copied into mimid at the revision above (crates/mls-didwebvh/tests/fixtures/dif-didwebvh-test-suite/).
  Only the logs the ts implementation produced are copied: it is the one implementation with a log in every scenario,
  and its logs end in a single LF as the draft's profile requires.

